node_modules/
dist/
# Every env file, whatever it is called. Listing them one by one meant the
# next one — .env.production, holding a production database password and R2
# keys — was tracked by default, which is the wrong way round for a file
# whose entire purpose is holding secrets.
.env
.env.*
# ...except the templates, which carry names and comments but never values.
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
*.sqlite
data/
.claude/
